{"audio": "1corinthians-11.opus", "duration_ms": 244461, "sentences": [{"start_ms": 0, "end_ms": 3960, "text": "1 Corinthians, Chapter Eleven."}, {"start_ms": 5340, "end_ms": 8741, "text": "You are to imitate me, just as I imitate Christ."}, {"start_ms": 9441, "end_ms": 16101, "text": "Now I commend you for remembering me in everything and for maintaining the traditions, just as I passed them on to you."}, {"start_ms": 16701, "end_ms": 24762, "text": "But I want you to understand that the head of every man is Christ, and the head of the woman is man, and the head of Christ is God."}, {"start_ms": 25722, "end_ms": 30143, "text": "Every man who prays or prophesies with his head covered dishonors his head."}, {"start_ms": 30723, "end_ms": 38563, "text": "And every woman who prays or prophesies with her head uncovered dishonors her head, for it is just as if her head were shaved."}, {"start_ms": 39363, "end_ms": 43044, "text": "If a woman does not cover her head, she should have her hair cut off."}, {"start_ms": 43664, "end_ms": 49164, "text": "And if it is shameful for a woman to have her hair cut or shaved off, she should cover her head."}, {"start_ms": 50224, "end_ms": 56845, "text": "A man ought not to cover his head, since he is the image and glory of God; but the woman is the glory of man."}, {"start_ms": 57545, "end_ms": 60865, "text": "For man did not come from woman, but woman from man."}, {"start_ms": 61425, "end_ms": 64906, "text": "Neither was man created for woman, but woman for man."}, {"start_ms": 65586, "end_ms": 70466, "text": "For this reason a woman ought to have a sign of authority on her head, because of the angels."}, {"start_ms": 71506, "end_ms": 77287, "text": "In the Lord, however, woman is not independent of man, nor is man independent of woman."}, {"start_ms": 78047, "end_ms": 82367, "text": "For just as woman came from man, so also man is born of woman."}, {"start_ms": 82927, "end_ms": 85027, "text": "But everything comes from God."}, {"start_ms": 85907, "end_ms": 90948, "text": "Judge for yourselves: Is it proper for a woman to pray to God with her head uncovered?"}, {"start_ms": 91648, "end_ms": 100509, "text": "Doesn’t nature itself teach you that if a man has long hair, it is a disgrace to him, but that if a woman has long hair, it is her glory?"}, {"start_ms": 101209, "end_ms": 103709, "text": "For long hair is given to her as a covering."}, {"start_ms": 104609, "end_ms": 110289, "text": "If anyone is inclined to dispute this, we have no other practice, nor do the churches of God."}, {"start_ms": 110970, "end_ms": 116730, "text": "In the following instructions I have no praise to offer, because your gatherings do more harm than good."}, {"start_ms": 117390, "end_ms": 123771, "text": "First of all, I hear that when you come together as a church, there are divisions among you, and in part I believe it."}, {"start_ms": 124431, "end_ms": 128791, "text": "And indeed, there must be differences among you to show which of you are approved."}, {"start_ms": 129511, "end_ms": 133972, "text": "Now then, when you come together, it is not the Lord’s Supper you eat."}, {"start_ms": 134552, "end_ms": 138532, "text": "For as you eat, each of you goes ahead without sharing his meal."}, {"start_ms": 139192, "end_ms": 141912, "text": "While one remains hungry, another gets drunk."}, {"start_ms": 142412, "end_ms": 145192, "text": "Don’t you have your own homes in which to eat and drink?"}, {"start_ms": 145793, "end_ms": 149953, "text": "Or do you despise the church of God and humiliate those who have nothing?"}, {"start_ms": 150693, "end_ms": 151753, "text": "What can I say to you?"}, {"start_ms": 152233, "end_ms": 153553, "text": "Shall I praise you for this?"}, {"start_ms": 154133, "end_ms": 155333, "text": "No, I will not!"}, {"start_ms": 156093, "end_ms": 169115, "text": "For I received from the Lord what I also passed on to you: The Lord Jesus, on the night He was betrayed, took bread, and when He had given thanks, He broke it and said, “This is My body, which is for you;"}, {"start_ms": 169735, "end_ms": 185356, "text": "do this in remembrance of Me.” In the same way, after supper He took the cup, saying, “This cup is the new covenant in My blood; do this, as often as you drink it, in remembrance of Me.” For as often as you eat this bread and drink this cup,"}, {"start_ms": 185736, "end_ms": 188216, "text": "you proclaim the Lord’s death until He comes."}, {"start_ms": 188976, "end_ms": 197577, "text": "Therefore, whoever eats the bread or drinks the cup of the Lord in an unworthy manner will be guilty of sinning against the body and blood of the Lord."}, {"start_ms": 198557, "end_ms": 202817, "text": "Each one must examine himself before he eats of the bread and drinks of the cup."}, {"start_ms": 203437, "end_ms": 209618, "text": "For anyone who eats and drinks without recognizing the body eats and drinks judgment on himself."}, {"start_ms": 210538, "end_ms": 215599, "text": "That is why many among you are weak and sick, and a number of you have fallen asleep."}, {"start_ms": 216399, "end_ms": 220859, "text": "Now if we judged ourselves properly, we would not come under judgment."}, {"start_ms": 221539, "end_ms": 227120, "text": "But when we are judged by the Lord, we are being disciplined so that we will not be condemned with the world."}, {"start_ms": 228040, "end_ms": 232280, "text": "So, my brothers, when you come together to eat, wait for one another."}, {"start_ms": 232860, "end_ms": 238600, "text": "If anyone is hungry, he should eat at home, so that when you come together it will not result in judgment."}, {"start_ms": 239221, "end_ms": 242861, "text": "And when I come, I will give instructions about the remaining matters."}], "words": [{"t": "1", "s": 0, "e": 2360, "si": 0}, {"t": "Corinthians,", "s": 2360, "e": 3000, "si": 0}, {"t": "Chapter", "s": 3200, "e": 3540, "si": 0}, {"t": "Eleven.", "s": 3580, "e": 3960, "si": 0}, {"t": "You", "s": 5340, "e": 5420, "si":